A game's window refits the screen when the Mac's display mode changes while it plays.

This repository's patch to win32u and winemac (version 2, after the S222 review), to be offered to WineHQ. It is
mavrik's own; nothing is copied. It uses upstream Wine's own machinery for emulated display modes (win32u's virtual and
raw monitor rects, map_window_rects_virt_to_raw and update_window_state, Wine 9 and later) and changes only when it
runs. Upstream Wine master (checked 2026-11-03: dlls/win32u/defwnd.c, dlls/winemac.drv/display.c and gdi.c, and
Proton's bleeding-edge and proton_10.0 defwnd.c) has the same code, so the fault is upstream's too, on X11 as on the
Mac.

The fault: with EmulateModeset=y, which mavrik sets in every prefix, a mode change made outside Wine (System
Settings' "Larger Text", another app, a display that changes its mode) keeps the game's virtual mode and changes
only the physical one (win32u add_modes). The desktop window's WM_DISPLAYCHANGE handler compared only the virtual
screen rect, found it unchanged and returned, so update_children_window_state never ran and every window kept its
old raw rect. In mavrik's S222 lab, switching a 14-inch MacBook Pro from 1512x982 to 1352x878 points for 20 s left
ABZU (DXMT) and Civ VI (D3DMetal) full screen at 0,0 1512x982 and Rogue Legacy (OpenGL) windowed at 76,75 1360x800,
so the picture was cut off at the right and bottom until the mode came back.

Now:
- win32u: the desktop also compares the raw virtual screen rect and, when it changed, updates its children's window
  state. Each window is mapped onto the new raw screen the way upstream maps a game's own emulated mode: a
  full-screen window gets the whole new raw monitor (stretched if the aspect ratio differs), and other windows scale
  with the screen around its centre, as a graphics card's scaler shows a mode on a panel of another size. The game
  sees no change: its mode, window rect and client size stay the same and no WM_DISPLAYCHANGE, WM_SIZE or
  WM_WINDOWPOSCHANGED reaches it, so it resets nothing. When only the raw screen changed, the cursor clip (kept in raw
  coordinates) is reset and the foreground window clipped again, as display_mode_changed does after a program's own
  mode change; otherwise a game holding the pointer would stay confined to the old raw rect. A clip the game set
  itself is dropped until the game sets it again, as upstream already does for its own mode changes.
- winemac: each GUI thread that gets a DISPLAYS_CHANGED event resets the process's device data (desktop rect, Retina
  state, the main display's size in millimetres) and reads it again through device_init, as
  macdrv_ChangeDisplaySettings already resets it after its own change, so with RetinaMode=y the monitors the desktop
  reads and the frames the game's process sets agree on the new mode (Retina mode is on only in the mode Wine started
  in; Wine bug 42973). macdrv_get_desktop_rect now calls device_init too, so the data is read once per change and
  marked valid.
Why scale rather than make the outside mode the game's new virtual mode: under an emulated mode the program's display
did not change, and telling a running game its display changed (WM_DISPLAYCHANGE, a new monitor size) makes many
games reset their device or leave full screen; the scaler keeps the game as it was and only its picture moves. On
Windows the system sends WM_DISPLAYCHANGE to every top-level window and the program decides.

Not covered: a Vulkan swapchain decides on present scaling when it is made (win32u vulkan.c), so after the refit the
game gets VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR; DXVK and most engines then make a new swapchain, and one that ignores it shows an
unscaled picture. Whether Wine's OpenGL drawable follows the smaller view is what the lab's Rogue Legacy row shows.

Checked (mavrik S222 lab): applies after patches 0001 to 0043 with no fuzz; win32u.so and winemac.so build with the
engine's toolchain and configure with no new warning, and without this patch both rebuild byte-identical to
revision 12's. The live resolution rows are run by the main session (lab-s222/res-patch/design.md).

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
index 4d55ed53..d81db061 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
@@ -3039,15 +3039,20 @@ LRESULT desktop_window_proc( HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wparam, LPARAM lparam,
         return 0;
     case WM_DISPLAYCHANGE:
     {
-        static RECT virtual_rect = {INT_MIN,INT_MIN,INT_MAX,INT_MAX};
+        static RECT virtual_rect = {INT_MIN,INT_MIN,INT_MAX,INT_MAX}, raw_rect = {INT_MIN,INT_MIN,INT_MAX,INT_MAX};
 
         RECT new_rect = get_virtual_screen_rect( 0, MDT_DEFAULT ), old_rect = virtual_rect;
+        RECT new_raw_rect = get_virtual_screen_rect( 0, MDT_RAW_DPI );
         UINT context, flags = 0;
 
-        if (EqualRect( &new_rect, &old_rect )) return TRUE;
+        /* With emulated display modes, a host mode change keeps the virtual screen and changes
+         * only the raw one: the windows still need mapping onto the new raw screen. */
+        if (EqualRect( &new_rect, &old_rect ) && EqualRect( &new_raw_rect, &raw_rect )) return TRUE;
         virtual_rect = new_rect;
+        raw_rect = new_raw_rect;
 
-        TRACE( "desktop %p change from %s to %s\n", hwnd, wine_dbgstr_rect( &old_rect ), wine_dbgstr_rect( &new_rect ) );
+        TRACE( "desktop %p change from %s to %s, raw %s\n", hwnd, wine_dbgstr_rect( &old_rect ),
+               wine_dbgstr_rect( &new_rect ), wine_dbgstr_rect( &new_raw_rect ) );
 
         if (new_rect.right - new_rect.left == old_rect.right - old_rect.left &&
             new_rect.bottom - new_rect.top == old_rect.bottom - old_rect.top)
@@ -3063,6 +3068,14 @@ LRESULT desktop_window_proc( HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wparam, LPARAM lparam,
 
         update_children_window_state( hwnd );
 
+        /* The cursor clip is kept in raw coordinates: reset it and clip the foreground
+         * window again, as a program's own mode change does (display_mode_changed). */
+        if (EqualRect( &new_rect, &old_rect ))
+        {
+            NtUserClipCursor( NULL );
+            NtUserPostMessage( NtUserGetForegroundWindow(), WM_WINE_CLIPCURSOR, SET_CURSOR_FSCLIP, 0 );
+        }
+
         return 0;
     }
     default:
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/display.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/display.c
index ba95f6ec..41566829 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/display.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/display.c
@@ -1087,6 +1087,12 @@ void macdrv_displays_changed(const macdrv_event *event)
 {
     HWND hwnd = NtUserGetDesktopWindow();
 
+    /* A change made outside Wine (System Settings, another app) leaves this process's
+       desktop rect and Retina state stale, so refresh them as ChangeDisplaySettings does
+       after its own change, before the monitors are read again (Wine bug 42973). */
+    macdrv_reset_device_metrics();
+    macdrv_get_desktop_rect();
+
     /* A system display change will get delivered to all GUI-attached threads,
        so the desktop-window-owning thread will get it and all others should
        ignore it.  A synthesized display change event due to activation
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
index 9cf415b5..a875ae0c 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
@@ -54,6 +54,8 @@ static pthread_mutex_t device_data_mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
 
 static const struct user_driver_funcs macdrv_funcs;
 
+static void device_init(void);
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *              compute_desktop_rect
  */
@@ -94,11 +96,7 @@ CGRect macdrv_get_desktop_rect(void)
 
     pthread_mutex_lock(&device_data_mutex);
 
-    if (!device_data_valid)
-    {
-        check_retina_status();
-        compute_desktop_rect();
-    }
+    if (!device_data_valid) device_init();
     ret = desktop_rect;
 
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&device_data_mutex);
